        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">08 &mdash; Timeline</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Monetization timeline: how long it takes</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">0-3 months: build content library and audience, no revenue</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">3-6 months: reach YPP threshold (with consistent posting), first payouts</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">6-12 months: meaningful ad revenue + brand deal opportunities</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4"><strong>Month 1-3: Foundation.</strong> Post 1-2 Shorts daily, experiment with formats, find your niche and voice. Most creators see 1,000-50,000 views per Short during this phase. Revenue: $0 (not yet eligible for YPP). Focus: learning what works, building a content library, and growing subscribers toward the 1,000 threshold.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4"><strong>Month 3-6: Growth.</strong> Formats are established, posting cadence is consistent, some Shorts start breaking out. Creators posting daily typically reach 1,000 subscribers during this phase. The 10M Shorts views threshold is harder and may take longer. Some creators get a viral hit that accelerates this. Revenue: $0-$50/month if you reach YPP early. Focus: hitting YPP thresholds and building brand deal opportunities.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4"><strong>Month 6-12: Monetization.</strong> YPP is active, ad revenue starts flowing, brand deal inquiries increase. With 5-10 million Shorts views per month, expect $100-$500/month from ad revenue. Brand deals and sponsorships can add $500-$5,000/month depending on niche and audience. Focus: optimizing RPM, diversifying revenue, and possibly adding long-form content.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4"><strong>Month 12+: Scale.</strong> Established format, growing audience, multiple revenue streams. Top Shorts creators earn $1,000-$5,000/month from ad revenue and $5,000-$50,000/month from brand deals, affiliates, and other monetization. Focus: scaling what works, building team support, and expanding to other platforms and formats.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">These timelines assume consistent daily posting and reasonable content quality. Creators in underserved niches or those who get early viral hits can accelerate significantly. Creators who post inconsistently or in highly competitive niches may take longer.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 09 Beyond Ads -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="beyond-ads">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">09 &mdash; Other Revenue</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Beyond ad revenue: other ways Shorts make money</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Brand sponsorships pay 5-50x more than ad revenue per view</li>
