        <h3 class="font-display text-[18px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.01em] text-ink mt-8 mb-3">Brand sponsorships</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Brand sponsorships are the biggest revenue driver for most Shorts creators. A creator with 100K subscribers and consistent viewership can charge $500-$3,000 per sponsored Short. A creator with 500K+ subscribers can charge $2,000-$10,000+. These rates dwarf ad revenue. A single sponsored Short can earn more than months of ad revenue. Building a sponsorship pipeline requires consistent content quality, audience demographics data, and proactive outreach or representation. For guidance on working with brands, see our <a href="/canvas-ugc/" class="text-accent hover:underline">Canvas UGC guide</a>.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display text-[18px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.01em] text-ink mt-8 mb-3">Affiliate marketing</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Affiliate links in Shorts descriptions or pinned comments can generate significant passive income, especially for product-focused niches (tech reviews, beauty, fitness equipment). Commission rates typically range from 3-15% of product price. A viral Short featuring a product can generate thousands of affiliate clicks and hundreds of sales.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display text-[18px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.01em] text-ink mt-8 mb-3">Super Thanks and fan funding</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">YouTube's Super Thanks feature lets viewers tip creators directly on Shorts. While individual tips are small ($2-$50), consistent creators can earn $100-$1,000/month from Super Thanks as their audience grows and engagement deepens. This feature is available to creators in the expanded YPP tier (500 subscribers + 3M Shorts views).</p>

        <h3 class="font-display text-[18px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.01em] text-ink mt-8 mb-3">Driving traffic to owned assets</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">The most scalable monetization strategy is using Shorts to drive traffic to higher-margin owned assets: online courses ($50-$500), coaching programs ($500-$5,000), digital downloads ($10-$100), and membership communities ($5-$50/month). A Short that attracts 100,000 views and converts 0.1% to a $100 product generates $10,000 &mdash; more than most creators earn from 100 million Shorts ad revenue views.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

